## Direct random-bunny disposition

Two independent direct processes used `SurfaceCells`, fallback `Fail`, recovery disabled, zero warmups, and one measured run. Both hit the 60-second guard before producing benchmark JSON:

- run 1: 60.05 s, 2,740,543,488 B peak RSS;
- run 2: 60.05 s, 2,740,506,624 B peak RSS;
- mean peak at timeout: 2,740,525,056 B (2.552 GiB).

A stage-7 injected run completed through simplification in 19.260599 s at 343,326,720 B with 21,298 arrangement and simplified cells. The production regression is therefore isolated to completion/ownership repair.

The previous `8595/8573` claim cannot be declared removed or reclassified because completion did not terminate and emitted no terminal conflict record.

## Diagnosis

The recursive same-corner candidate path can branch at each depth, copy the full complex, and rerun parity, descriptor derivation, every patch completion, and assembly. Its limits are depth-local rather than one shared global work budget, and equivalent repair states are not memoized. The deterministic 60-second/2.74-GB behavior is a production-blocking completion-stage time and memory runaway.

Test-integrity gap: current tests validate stitch-time `SameCornerDistinctBoundaryClaim` classification, but no test invokes `complete_surface_cell_complex()` and verifies bounded `BoundarySectorSubdivision` behavior or structural-attempt diagnostics.

## Required next code/build turn

Use `.agents/Directional/Milestone_G_P5_Bounded_Structural_Repair_Code_Build_Plan.md`.

- [ ] Replace recursive candidate-tree expansion with one globally bounded deterministic repair ledger.
- [ ] Add collision-safe canonical repair-state memoization.
- [ ] Keep at most one candidate complex and rollback snapshot live at a time.
- [ ] Require strict monotonic progress and prohibit replacing one ownership conflict with another.
- [ ] Fail invalid overlap before candidate search.
- [ ] Reuse unaffected descriptor/completion products where equivalence is provable.
- [ ] Add real whole-complex structural-repair tests, budget tests, repeated-state tests, and diagnostics coverage.
- [ ] Compile only the four required targets and run no tests, benchmarks, or custom meshes.

